<title>SWEDEN: Swedish airports move 5 pct more cargo in April.</title>
<headline>Swedish airports move 5 pct more cargo in April.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish airports handled five percent more cargo in April than a year earlier, Sweden's civil aviation administration Luftfartsverket said on Friday.</p>
<p>State-owned Luftfartsverket, which owns 14 civil airports and operates five other civil and military airports in Sweden, published the following figures about April airport activity.</p>
<p>The cargo figures do not include trucked air freight.</p>
<p>					  APRIL		 JAN-APRIL</p>
<p>				  1997	 1996	1997	1996</p>
<p> Cargo (in tonnes)	 13,551     12,905    51,705    45,111</p>
<p> Mail (in tonnes)	   3,956	3,451    12,155    10,501</p>
<p> Landings		    30,654     29,107   109,506   106,531</p>
<p> Passengers (in millions) 1.621	1.409     5.791     5.377</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
